(3) When discussing or deliberating upon the appointment, employment, compensation, hiring, disciplinary action or dismissal, or periodic evaluation or rating of a public officer or employee, but not when receiving evidence or hearing argument on charges filed to determine disciplinary action or dismissal of a public officer or employee. The vote on any matter covered by this subsection shall be taken in public and minutes of the meeting as provided in the Open and Public Meetings laws (O.C.G.A. § 50-14-1 et seq.) shall be made available. Meetings to discuss or take action on the filling of a vacancy in the membership of the City Council, or a department thereof shall at all times be open to the public as provided in the Open and Public Meetings laws (O.C.G.A. § 50-14-1 et seq.);
(4) Hearings or discussions on the discipline or removal of any public official unless the official requests that the meeting or a portion thereof be open to the public, whereupon the meeting or a portion thereof shall be open;
