The City Attorney, or assistants under his/her direction, shall be the legal advisor and representative of the City and in that capacity shall:
(1) Advise any Council Member or the City Manager, when thereto requested, upon all legal questions arising in the conduct of the City business;
(2) Prepare or revise ordinances when so requested by the City Council or the City Manager and keep the Code of Ordinances of the City up-to-date and properly indexed;
(3) Give his/her official opinion upon any legal matter or question submitted by a majority vote of the City Council or the City Manager;
(4) Attend any Council meetings upon request of any member for the purpose of giving the City Council any legal advice requested by its members;
(5) Prepare for execution all contracts and instruments to which the City is a party when so requested and approve, as to form, all bonds and City contracts;
(6) Prepare, when authorized by the City Council, charges and complaints against, and appear in the Municipal Court in the prosecution of persons charged with a violation of this Code or of any regulations and see to the full enforcement of all civil judgments or decrees rendered or entered in favor of the City;
(7) Defend any and all suits and actions at law or equity brought against the City, unless otherwise directed by the City Council;
(8) Prepare and file any civil suit or action at law or equity to secure or protect the City's best interest when so directed by the Council or City Manager;
(9) Make immediate report to the City Council and City Manager of the outcome of any litigation in which the City has a direct interest;
